    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline's `audit` step emitted only a human-readable audit line. I added an **immutable structured event** alongside it, emitted via the same `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`: a `record` (deeply immutable) with fields `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}` and the `OWNER_CREATED` constant.\n\n**Updated** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Keeps the existing audit line unchanged (\"in addition to the audit line\").\n- Emits a second `AUDIT.info` line: the event serialized to JSON via Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`), e.g.\n  `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n- `seq` comes from a `static final AtomicLong`, so it's **monotonically increasing across every create** (shared state, not per-request).\n- The identifier value is sourced through a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `customerCode` today. That is the one point to change when the customerCode is unified into the memberId \u2014 the event's identifier then carries the memberId with no other edit, exactly as the spec (and the test's forward-looking comment about \"the event switched to the memberId\") anticipates.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` test \u2014 which asserts one `AUDIT` line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the `customerCode` \u2014 now passes, and the full suite is green.",
